            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RMSR"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Good in a pinch, but I prefer the more authentic tasting versions. Nevertheless, it served its purpose well and tasted fine. I made a half batch to serve with salmon cakes. I used Dijon mustard instead of the yellow, splash of pickle juice for the lemon juice, added some chopped up bread &amp; butter pickles, a bit of lemon pepper and tarragon. Definitely let this sit in the fridge a few hours to meld the flavours.",
            "datePublished": "2011-07-01T19:49:40.210Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TwistyBrie1042"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Giving this a 4, because it inspired me to make a much better version: 1 giant tbsp of dijon 1 whole egg 1.5 tsp apple cider vinegar 1 cup canola oil 4-5 capers 1/2 a minced pickle 1 tbsp lemon juice 1/2 tsp salt 1/2 tsp pepper Blend in immersion blender. Lasts a week in fridge. Enjoy. This is ridiculously good. Technically more of a mayo than a tartar...but the dijon works as excellent substitute for the horseradish, so call it whatever you want. Thank you for the inspiration!",
            "datePublished": "2024-02-08T01:29:07.682Z"
